## ⚠️ Scope — design system ONLY

This context maintains the **{{SYSTEM_NAME}} design system itself** — tokens, styles, components, variants,
bindings, the manifest, skills docs, publish hygiene, drift, and the spiels mechanism. All DS work
happens *inside Figma* (the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} SOURCE) via the `use_figma` tool, which **requires the Figma Desktop
Bridge** (Figma desktop app open + bridge plugin running). If the bridge is NOT available, **STOP and
tell the user** — never fall back to writing code.

**Out of scope — a SEPARATE context owns these:** building / recreating consumer *screens*, flows /
IA / specs, and coded prototypes (React / Next / HTML / Storybook). This context publishes {{SYSTEM_NAME}} +
updates `skills/`+`manifest/`; the separate screen-creation context consumes the published library to
build. A {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap found while building a screen comes back here as a tokenization / component request.

**Hard rule:** never emit React / HTML / coded output here. Screen building and prototypes live in the
other context — point the user there.

