## Critical rules (always)

1. **Plugin API cannot publish a library** — user must click "Publish Library" in Figma UI
2. **`use_figma` requires font loading** — load all {{FONTS}} weights before any text op
3. **Render-verify after every visual change** — call `figma_get_component_image` to confirm
4. **Always offer to update skills/manifest** when {{SYSTEM_NAME}} changes happen — drift kills the system
5. **Honest scope notes always** — if a workaround is needed, say so explicitly
6. **Anchor frame pattern for centered text** — when a layout has toggleable side slots with centered middle content, wrap each side in a fixed-size anchor frame (see figma-gotchas).
7. **URL node-IDs may resolve to pages, not components** — when `figma_get_component` returns `type: "CANVAS"`, scan children for the real COMPONENT_SET (see figma-gotchas).
8. **Variants must live inside their component_set's bounds** — orphaned variants render via direct API call but get suppressed in the variant picker UI (see figma-gotchas).
9. **Audit bindings before publish** — run the binding audit script on any component built via `use_figma`. Target zero unbound elements. `clone()` does NOT carry variable bindings reliably; re-bind after cloning.
10. **Never fall back to code** — design-system work is Figma (`use_figma`) via the Desktop Bridge. If the bridge is unavailable, STOP and tell the user. Coded prototypes + screen building are out of scope here — they live in the separate screen-creation context. See the Scope gate at the top.

## Communication format

User prefers structured responses with `yaml` code blocks for planning and decision points. Inline prose for execution and explanation. NO tappable buttons / `ask_user_input_v0` — straight conversation only.

